    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Tails is the 1995 debut studio album by Lisa Loeb & Nine Stories, originally released on Geffen Records and later reissued here in the 2026 Neon Flamingo Translucent edition. Built around Loeb’s literate songwriting and clear, intimate vocal style, the album sits in the pop lane while drawing from acoustic rock and alt-pop textures, with songs that balance sweetness, tension, and a conversational emotional directness.\n\nThe album’s best-known track, “Stay (I Missed You),” helped define Loeb’s breakthrough, while “Do You Sleep?” and “Taffy” extended its radio presence and helped the record reach Gold certification in the U.S. Produced with Juan Patiño and recorded in New York, Tails has long been valued for its understated arrangements and confessional tone, and this translucent neon vinyl reissue revives one of mid-’90s pop’s most recognizable and enduring debuts.",
